,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-17T18:34:35Z","updated_at":"2025-01-17T18:34:35Z","body":"Maybe from? https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/96099 it seems that prior to dev2 the noise texture didn't actually regenerate at all","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2598971024/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2598980355","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101544#issuecomment-2598980355","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101544","id":2598980355,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6a6UsD","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-17T18:39:21Z","updated_at":"2025-01-17T18:39:21Z","body":"I confirmed that enabling thread support in the export options brings the FPS back up to normal!\n\nFor context for OP. 4.3 introduced an option to run web exports without multithreading. NoiseTexture generates the texture in the background so that it doesn't impact FPS (but that causes a delay in when it updates). In 4.3+ we default to not using threads on web exports. In 4.3 and in dev 1 this meant that NoiseTextures just didn't update at all. In dev2 we fixed that bug, but that means that on single threaded web exports the texture has to be generated on the main thread and it is really slow, so it causes the low FPS. \n\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2598980355/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2599033123","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101544#issuecomment-2599033123","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101544","id":2599033123,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6a6hkj","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-17T19:15:32Z","updated_at":"2025-01-17T19:15:32Z","body":"CC @adamscott @Calinou - we should at least document that on Web single threaded NoiseTextures are very costly and should be baked.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2599033123/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2599463364","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101544#issuecomment-2599463364","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101544","id":2599463364,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6a8KnE","user":{"login":"FeralBytes","id":7874274,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4NzQyNzQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7874274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes","html_url":"https://github.com/FeralBytes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-18T01:52:29Z","updated_at":"2025-01-18T01:52:29Z","body":"@clayjohn Thank you for the explanation. I assume that you mean 4.4. \n@akien-mga how do I bake a noise texture? Do I save it as a tres. Or try to save it as a png? I attempted to save the resource but .tres was the only option and it was still a fast noise resource any ways. Thank you for your time. This is definitely something that I need to know how to do in order to better optimize in the future.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2599463364/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2599468496","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101544#issuecomment-2599468496","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101544","id":2599468496,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6a8L3Q","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-18T02:00:33Z","updated_at":"2025-01-18T02:00:55Z","body":"> [@clayjohn](https://github.com/clayjohn) Thank you for the explanation. I assume that you mean 4.4.\n\nNope, 4.3. https://godotengine.org/releases/4.3/#highlights-single-threaded-web-export\n\nThe fact that 4.3 wasn't slow was a bug that got fixed in 4.4 dev2\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2599468496/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2616889294","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101544#issuecomment-2616889294","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101544","id":2616889294,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6b-o_O","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-27T21:04:03Z","updated_at":"2025-01-27T21:04:18Z","body":"> how do I bake a noise texture? Do I save it as a tres. Or try to save it as a png? I attempted to save the resource but .tres was the only option and it was still a fast noise resource any ways. Thank you for your time. This is definitely something that I need to know how to do in order to better optimize in the future.\n\nThis is not possible yet without a script that reads all the Image's pixels and saves them a PNG or similar. See https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/7023.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2616889294/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2617128940","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101544#issuecomment-2617128940","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101544","id":2617128940,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6b_jfs","user":{"login":"FeralBytes","id":7874274,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4NzQyNzQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7874274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes","html_url":"https://github.com/FeralBytes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeralBytes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-27T23:30:20Z","updated_at":"2025-01-27T23:33:46Z","body":"@Calinou Thank you for taking the time to respond. \nI spent some time and researched this some today. And I built a little tool script that saves the noise texture as a .png as an optimization for the web. It is very particular in that it expects it's parent to have a material shader and for the shader to have a parameter named noise_tex but other than that it works very well. \n\n`Note: Godot does not immediately see the new file, switch to another program and then back and it will see the new PNG.\n\n```gdscript\n@tool\nextends Node\n\n@export_tool_button(\"Save Noise Texture\") var save_action = save_noise_texture\n@export_dir var save_path_folder:String = \"res://assets/images/noise_textures/\"\n@export var save_file_name:String = \"Noise1\"\n\nfunc _ready():\n    print(\"Noise Baker is ready to save some noise.\")\n\nfunc save_noise_texture() -> void:\n    print(\"Baking the noise texture now...\")\n    var img = get_parent().material.get_shader_parameter(\"noise_tex\").get_image()\n    img.clear_mipmaps()\n    img.save_png(save_path_folder + save_file_name + \".png\")\n    print(\"Saved noise texture to path of: \" + save_path_folder + save_file_name + \".png\")\n```\n\nI must say that I really like your idea from the proposal of using a hash for the file name. I may implement that in the future.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2617128940/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]